uutils is a family of cross-platform reimplementations of the GNU
utilities, written in Rust.  This is a meta-package that installs the
uutils-coreutils, uutils-findutils, uutils-diffutils, uutils-grep,
uutils-awk, uutils-sed and uutils-tar packages.

Each of those packages provides the same file names as the GNU port it
replaces, so ports that depend on sysutils/coreutils, misc/findutils,
textproc/gdiff, sysutils/ggrep, lang/gawk, textproc/gsed or
archivers/gtar only need their build dependency pointed at the matching
uutils package.  The packages declare the appropriate @conflict and
@pkgpath entries and must not be installed together with their GNU
counterpart.
